  "question": {
    "text": "A Carnot engine whose low-temperature reservoir is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>350</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> has an efficiency of <math><mn>50</mn><mi>%</mi></math> . It is desired to increase the efficiency to <math><mn>60</mn><mi>%</mi></math>. If the temperature of the low-temperature reservoir is kept constant, then by how many kelvins the temperature of the high-temperature reservoir must be increased to get the desired efficiency?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "175",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The efficiency of the Carnot engine,</p><p><math><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p>When <math><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>%</mi></math></p><p>then <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>350</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>700</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p>When <math><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mi>%</mi></math></p><p>then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>0.6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>350</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>875</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p>Hence, the temperature of the high reservoir is increased by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>&#8242;</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>875</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>700</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>175</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p>"
  }
}